{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) has assigned stitch task #5249 from generation-run44. This is an automated code generation task within the go-unix-utils project. The task requires:\n   - Reviewing the provided project context (SRDs, architecture, source code, package contracts)\n   - Reading `.cobbler/requirements.yaml` to determine which specific requirements are assigned to this task\n   - Implementing the assigned requirements (creating/modifying Go source files)\n   - Verifying the implementation compiles and passes tests\n   - NOT running any git commands (managed externally by orchestrator)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils verified via differential testing\n   - Cobbler scaffold pipeline: measure (task planning) → stitch (code generation)\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary vs Homebrew GNU reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handler pattern via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for all cmd/ utilities\n   - Package contracts defining exported types/functions for shared pkg/ libraries\n   - Requirement states tracking (ready/in_progress/code_complete) for each SRD requirement\n   - Strict execution constitution: 40-line function limit, 500-line file limit, copyright headers, no scope creep\n   - Write-first strategy: write all files before building/testing\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `.cobbler/requirements.yaml` — Contains the task assignments mapping requirements to task IDs. Attempted to read but FAILED due to 30716 token limit. This is the critical file needed to determine what to implement.\n   - Existing pkg/ source code provided inline:\n     - `pkg/encutil/decode.go` and `pkg