{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011WnZeQrP3u4uWpi4wvrY5Y","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (306.6KB). Full output saved to: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5249/79ade233-2351-439e-b2bb-3fc96fcc4b96/tool-results/b7c78oce0.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\nNot found with plain grep\n/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5249/.cobbler/history/2026-05-14-12-44-40-measure-log.log:5:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":384607,\"duration_api_ms\":387971,\"num_turns\":1,\"result\":\"## Project State Summary\\n\\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge on edge cases. This project derives formal specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI code generation, and verifies output parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\\n\\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify). Human-authored SRDs drive AI code generation via mage-claude-orchestrator. Go implementations live in `cmd/`, shared infrastructure in `pkg/` (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil). Differential testing compares Go and Homebrew GNU binaries byte-for-byte.\\n\\n**Current State**: All pkg/ infrastructure is implemented. Implemented cmd/ utilities: sponge, du, true, false, yes, basename, dirname, tee, head, seq, wc. Run 44 is active on branch `generation-run44`. Releases 00.0 through 03.0 are complete or have no ready requirements remaining.\\n\\n**Current Release**: Release 03.1 (system information: uname, arch, nproc, hostname, hostid) is the earliest release with all requirements in `ready` state.\\n\\n## Priority Analysis\\n\\nRelease 03.1 contains 5 trivial system information utilities. Ordered by complexity: arch (7 reqs), hostid (7 reqs), hostname (7 reqs), nproc (10 reqs), uname (16 reqs). All have `ready` status on every requirement. Dependencies are minimal -- just pkg/sys for SIGPIPE handling.\\n\\nWith a 4-task limit and 4 sub-requirements per task, I propose core implementation tasks (R1/R2 groups) for the 4 simplest utilities. Testing/edge-case tasks (R3+ groups) follow in the next batch per P2 (split implementat\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79ade233-2351-439e-b2bb-3fc96fcc4b96","uuid":"ba760007-b00f-46dc-b440-409ac8311510","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:49:52.791Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Not found with plain grep\n/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5249/.cobbler/history/2026-05-14-12-44-40-measure-log.log:5:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":384607,\"duration_api_ms\":387971,\"num_turns\":1,\"result\":\"## Project State Summary\\n\\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge on edge cases. This project derives formal specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI code generation, and verifies output parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\\n\\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify). Human-authored SRDs drive AI code generation via mage-claude-orchestrator. Go implementations live in `cmd/`, shared infrastructure in `pkg/` (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil). Differential testing compares Go and Homebrew GNU binaries byte-for-byte.\\n\\n**Current State**: All pkg/ infrastructure is implemented. Implemented cmd/ utilities: sponge, du, true, false, yes, basename, dirname, tee, head, seq, wc. Run 44 is active on branch `generation-run44`. Releases 00.0 through 03.0 are complete or have no ready requirements remaining.\\n\\n**Current Release**: Release 03.1 (system information: uname, arch, nproc, hostname, hostid) is the earliest release with all requirements in `ready` state.\\n\\n## Priority Analysis\\n\\nRelease 03.1 contains 5 trivial system information utilities. Ordered by complexity: arch (7 reqs), hostid (7 reqs), hostname (7 reqs), nproc (10 reqs), uname (16 reqs). All have `ready` status on every requirement. Dependencies are minimal -- just pkg/sys for SIGPIPE handling.\\n\\nWith a 4-task limit and 4 sub-requirements per task, I propose core implementation tasks (R1/R2 groups) for the 4 simplest utilities. Testing/edge-case tasks (R3+ groups) follow in the next batch per P2 (split implementation and tests) and P8 (implementation before tests).\\n\\n## Weight Budget Check\\n\\nWeights assumed default 1 per requirement (cannot read requirements.yaml per constraints).\\n\\n- Task 0: srd045-arch R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4\\n- Task 1: srd048-hostid R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4\\n- Task 2: srd047-hostname R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4\\n- Task 3: srd046-nproc R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R1.3 (w=1) + R1.4 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4\\n\\n## Proposed Tasks\\n\\n```yaml\\n- index: 0\\n  title: \\\"[stitch] cmd/arch: core implementation and error handling (srd045-arch R1.1-R1.2, R2.1-R2.2)\\\"\\n  dependency: -1\\n  description: |\\n    deliverable_type: code\\n\\n    required_reading:\\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd045-arch.yaml (full SRD for arch)\\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage and existing syscall wrappers)\\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared protocols and import constraints)\\n\\n    files:\\n      - path: cmd/arch/main.go\\n        action: create\\n        note: arch utility -- prints machine hardware name to stdout\\n\\n    requirements:\\n      - id: R1\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd045-arch R1.1 -- print the machine hardware name to stdout\\\"\\n      - id: R2\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd045-arch R1.2 -- output formatting and newline termination\\\"\\n      - id: R3\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd045-arch R2.1 -- --help flag prints usage to stdout and exits 0\\\"\\n      - id: R4\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd045-arch R2.2 -- --version flag prints version to stdout and exits 0\\\"\\n\\n    design_decisions:\\n      - id: D1\\n        text: \\\"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start of main per shared protocol\\\"\\n      - id: D2\\n        text: \\\"Per architecture, cmd/ packages must not import golang.org/x/sys directly -- route platform syscalls through pkg/sys or use Go standard library\\\"\\n\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: AC1\\n        text: \\\"go build -o bin/arch ./cmd/arch/ succeeds without errors\\\"\\n      - id: AC2\\n        text: \\\"go vet ./cmd/arch/ reports no issues\\\"\\n      - id: AC3\\n        text: \\\"bin/arch prints the machine hardware name followed by a newline\\\"\\n      - id: AC4\\n        text: \\\"bin/arch --help prints usage information and exits 0\\\"\\n      - id: AC5\\n        text: \\\"bin/arch --version prints version information and exits 0\\\"\\n\\n- index: 1\\n  title: \\\"[stitch] cmd/hostid: core implementation and error handling (srd048-hostid R1.1-R1.2, R2.1-R2.2)\\\"\\n  dependency: -1\\n  description: |\\n    deliverable_type: code\\n\\n    required_reading:\\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd048-hostid.yaml (full SRD for hostid)\\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared protocols and import constraints)\\n\\n    files:\\n      - path: cmd/hostid/main.go\\n        action: create\\n        note: hostid utility -- prints 32-bit host identifier as 8-digit hex\\n\\n    requirements:\\n      - id: R1\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd048-hostid R1.1 -- print the 32-bit host identifier as an 8-digit zero-padded lowercase hexadecimal number\\\"\\n      - id: R2\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd048-hostid R1.2 -- output terminated with a trailing newline\\\"\\n      - id: R3\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd048-hostid R2.1 -- --help flag prints usage to stdout and exits 0\\\"\\n      - id: R4\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd048-hostid R2.2 -- --version flag prints version to stdout and exits 0\\\"\\n\\n    design_decisions:\\n      - id: D1\\n        text: \\\"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start of main per shared protocol\\\"\\n      - id: D2\\n        text: \\\"Per architecture, cmd/ packages must not import golang.org/x/sys directly -- route platform syscalls through pkg/sys or use Go standard library\\\"\\n\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: AC1\\n        text: \\\"go build -o bin/hostid ./cmd/hostid/ succeeds without errors\\\"\\n      - id: AC2\\n        text: \\\"go vet ./cmd/hostid/ reports no issues\\\"\\n      - id: AC3\\n        text: \\\"bin/hostid prints an 8-digit hexadecimal number followed by a newline\\\"\\n      - id: AC4\\n        text: \\\"bin/hostid --help prints usage information and exits 0\\\"\\n      - id: AC5\\n        text: \\\"bin/hostid --version prints version information and exits 0\\\"\\n\\n- index: 2\\n  title: \\\"[stitch] cmd/hostname: core implementation and error handling (srd047-hostname R1.1-R1.2, R2.1-R2.2)\\\"\\n  dependency: -1\\n  description: |\\n    deliverable_type: code\\n\\n    required_reading:\\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd047-hostname.yaml (full SRD for hostname)\\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared protocols)\\n\\n    files:\\n      - path: cmd/hostname/main.go\\n        action: create\\n        note: hostname utility -- prints the system hostname\\n\\n    requirements:\\n      - id: R1\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd047-hostname R1.1 -- print the system hostname to stdout\\\"\\n      - id: R2\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd047-hostname R1.2 -- output terminated with a trailing newline\\\"\\n      - id: R3\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd047-hostname R2.1 -- --help flag prints usage to stdout and exits 0\\\"\\n      - id: R4\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd047-hostname R2.2 -- --version flag prints version to stdout and exits 0\\\"\\n\\n    design_decisions:\\n      - id: D1\\n        text: \\\"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start of main per shared protocol\\\"\\n\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: AC1\\n        text: \\\"go build -o bin/hostname ./cmd/hostname/ succeeds without errors\\\"\\n      - id: AC2\\n        text: \\\"go vet ./cmd/hostname/ reports no issues\\\"\\n      - id: AC3\\n        text: \\\"bin/hostname prints the system hostname followed by a newline\\\"\\n      - id: AC4\\n        text: \\\"bin/hostname --help prints usage information and exits 0\\\"\\n      - id: AC5\\n        text: \\\"bin/hostname --version prints version information and exits 0\\\"\\n\\n- index: 3\\n  title: \\\"[stitch] cmd/nproc: core implementation (srd046-nproc R1.1-R1.4)\\\"\\n  dependency: -1\\n  description: |\\n    deliverable_type: code\\n\\n    required_reading:\\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd046-nproc.yaml (full SRD for nproc)\\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared protocols)\\n\\n    files:\\n      - path: cmd/nproc/main.go\\n        action: create\\n        note: nproc utility -- prints number of available processing units\\n\\n    requirements:\\n      - id: R1\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd046-nproc R1.1 -- print the number of available processing units to stdout\\\"\\n      - id: R2\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd046-nproc R1.2 -- --all flag prints total number of installed processors\\\"\\n      - id: R3\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd046-nproc R1.3 -- --ignore=N flag subtracts N from the count with a minimum result of 1\\\"\\n      - id: R4\\n        text: \\\"Implement srd046-nproc R1.4 -- output terminated with a trailing newline\\\"\\n\\n    design_decisions:\\n      - id: D1\\n        text: \\\"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start of main per shared protocol\\\"\\n\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: AC1\\n        text: \\\"go build -o bin/nproc ./cmd/nproc/ succeeds without errors\\\"\\n      - id: AC2\\n        text: \\\"go vet ./cmd/nproc/ reports no issues\\\"\\n      - id: AC3\\n        text: \\\"bin/nproc prints a positive integer followed by a newline\\\"\\n      - id: AC4\\n        text: \\\"bin/nproc --all prints the total processor count\\\"\\n      - id: AC5\\n        text: \\\"bin/nproc --ignore=1 prints one less than the default count, minimum 1\\\"\\n```\\n\\nFour implementation tasks covering the core functionality of the four simplest utilities in release 03.1. Testing/edge-case tasks (R3 groups for arch, hostid, hostname; R2-R3 groups for nproc) and the full uname implementation (16 requirements) will follow in subsequent batches.\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"56d360c5-caaf-4570-9d66-2767d8432a83\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.0235524999999999,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":58184,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":11841,\"output_tokens\":24238,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":58184,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":2,\"output_tokens\":24238,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":11841,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":58184,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":58184},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":47807,\"outputTokens\":43,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.048022,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-opus-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":2,\"outputTokens\":24238,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":11841,\"cacheCreationInputToken